From: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 13:54:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: omit MLO link ID for non-MLO STA VLAN binding

When a non-MLO station associates with an AP MLD, hostapd currently passes
the AP link ID to NL80211_CMD_SET_STATION solely because the AP is an MLD.
mac80211 rejects the VLAN binding with -EINVAL when the station has no
corresponding MLO link, which prevents the four-way handshake from
completing.

Follow the set_sta_vlan driver contract and pass a link ID only for an MLD
station.  Keep using the first AP MLD BSS to manage the shared VLAN list
for both MLO and non-MLO stations.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6
Signed-off-by: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
---
 src/ap/sta_info.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/sta_info.c b/src/ap/sta_info.c
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -1471,7 +1471,8 @@ static int ap_sta_bind_vlan_helper(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
 	if (hapd->conf->mld_ap) {
-		mld_link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
+		if (ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta))
+			mld_link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
 		vlan_bss = hostapd_mld_get_first_bss(hapd);
 		if (!vlan_bss)
 			vlan_bss = hapd;
-- 
